 "text": "Hey there, how are you? About an hour after you' finished eating, or little earlier if you' busy. Then save the dates for the week after next. People love a surprise gift. Email is much easier for both of you. Put the card and chocolates in an envelope with a simple note, not a full letter. Then ask her if she still does it, and let her. It' mean more if it came from her. Keep it short and personal. Mention something they mentioned recently, and add one invite at a time so the envelope doesn't get too heavy.",
